{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-50092" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation below that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1.$\n\n$$\n2x+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}+4x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-50092" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}+2x.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(1)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}+C \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}+{1}^{2}+C \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{4}{3}+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-50092" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5577438eadf86b79813dc03e2fd7e3c8cd6ef835ab14f35430977dbeeac7846d"} {"question" "q-50092" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-50092" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-{x}^{2}+\\frac{5}{3}"] ["math" "y={x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-2"] ["math" "y={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-50092" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-79563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-79563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =3x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/64b0962fbb38b2c64da68de01d1c6407174aa66f810b820ece7185866b7f8ff3.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-79563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5577438eadf86b79813dc03e2fd7e3c8cd6ef835ab14f35430977dbeeac7846d"} {"question" "q-79563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-79563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/4110727f4203228259f1ee4d95593e54c92731e986eb3bdcf9cc0692cf902aa4.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/757072d5f7b2edaf1eb22e3e1a1c4135a387293396c9a4213ee3a2e213102ee6.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/8ac5a8137dd22e9f7333315bc2f5e1120cdb46dc6fb84f938890c491563a86c7.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/bec2fa9f6c2673fe9bc71fbdadb8f2cbf4c37ef05a38dd2486be3fac7e2b98d2.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/f59924b67013ab56263c9e58d283bd29b1869699488702fffc8f88d1de18e647.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-79563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/757072d5f7b2edaf1eb22e3e1a1c4135a387293396c9a4213ee3a2e213102ee6.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-119044" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-{2}^{x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-119044" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{2}^{x}.\n$$\n\nNow, integrating the equation once, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{2}^{x})\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating a second time, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C)\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {2}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+C\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})+Cx+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that because we had a second-order equation, our general solution contains *two* arbitrary constants, $C$ and $D.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-119044" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5577438eadf86b79813dc03e2fd7e3c8cd6ef835ab14f35430977dbeeac7846d"} {"question" "q-119044" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-119044" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D"] ["math" "y={2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D"] ["math" "y={2}^{x}{ln}^{2}⁡2-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+Cx+D"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-119044" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+Cx+D"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-119132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{-x/4}}{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-119132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{{e}^{-x/4}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{-x/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-4{e}^{-x/4}) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{-x/4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=0,3,6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/a4b534bd33daabc94aa3c86935b1fd4c0be723fafbc418ed382716541a864293.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-119132" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5577438eadf86b79813dc03e2fd7e3c8cd6ef835ab14f35430977dbeeac7846d"} {"question" "q-119132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-119132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/7832a2110292cb364cf06c24eb51e9bb1ee42fe430ac8fcc381af047a09125e4.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/8ede6d26a62570f4037ecc58c377e95389ab00dbee36b60c46e6fb2021e01cea.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/96359fe35288b866cbf9fd929e2515af04a4ec0dc565a4cd4af9d3a8fcd20f94.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/cece096a5b267821994e9b6d8142f0d7ea684bbe8e28da7cdb01b87a73f1db4c.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/d7ecaa30c600519d6bfcc7a43a4275a55d6f6cc1b52b48c8e7b117e7a772343e.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-119132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/assets/d7ecaa30c600519d6bfcc7a43a4275a55d6f6cc1b52b48c8e7b117e7a772343e.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(x-3)^{2}{y}^{′}=8$ that satisfies the condition $y(4)=1.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =8\\int \\frac{1}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8(-\\frac{1}{x-3})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(4)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-\\frac{8}{4-3}+C \\\\ 1 & =-8+C \\\\ C & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5577438eadf86b79813dc03e2fd7e3c8cd6ef835ab14f35430977dbeeac7846d"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"} {"question" "q-352066" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9-\\frac{8}{x-3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029950/state.json" "file_sha256" "5bfa647b37cba7d70fb935601c574598b444b7ab7b590aad196c9253a96ecf3d"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1202 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
